{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:43:20.177174Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Here are the one-stop options departing New York **after 11 AM EST** on May 20th, with economy seats available (prices are per passenger, total for both segments):\n\n| Routing | Depart NY | Arrive SEA | Economy Total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| JFK → ATL → SEA (HAT136 + HAT039) | 19:00 | 03:00 (+1) | $255 |\n| JFK → ATL → SEA (HAT218 + HAT039) | 18:00 | 03:00 (+1) | $261 |\n| EWR → DFW → SEA (HAT231 + HAT067) | 16:00 | 03:00 (+1) | $320 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT002 + HAT156) | 21:00 | 10:00 (+1) | $287 |\n\nA few notes:\n- HAT218 only has 1 economy seat remaining.\n- The JFK→ATL→SEA options have a fairly tight connection in Atlanta (~30 minutes).\n\nWhich option would you like? And how many passengers will be traveling?"}, "resultat": "I'll be the only passenger. I prefer direct flights, but one stopover is fine. Is there anything cheaper, even with one stop, that departs after 11 AM EST?", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 11, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:43:25.533820Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I checked all one-stop itineraries departing New York after 11:00 AM EST on May 20th with economy availability. The complete set of economy totals is:\n\n| Routing | Depart NY | Economy Total |\n|---|---|---|\n| **JFK → ATL → SEA (HAT136 + HAT039)** | **19:00** | **$255** ← cheapest |\n| JFK → ATL → SEA (HAT218 + HAT039) | 18:00 | $261 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT002 + HAT156) | 21:00 | $287 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT002 + HAT045) | 21:00 | $295 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT114 + HAT156) | 21:00 | $298 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT114 + HAT045) | 21:00 | $306 |\n| LGA → PHX → SEA (HAT002 + HAT251) | 21:00 | $310 |\n| EWR → DFW → SEA (HAT231 + HAT067) | 16:00 | $320 |\n\nSo **$255 for HAT136 (JFK 19:00 → ATL 21:30) + HAT039 (ATL 22:00 → SEA 03:00 +1)** is the cheapest option departing after 11 AM. (Note the ~30-minute connection in Atlanta.)\n\nWould you like to book that one?"}, "resultat": "Yes, I'll book the HAT136 + HAT039 option for $255.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 12, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:43:29.416493Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Great choice! Before I book, I need to confirm a few details:\n\n1. **Passenger name and date of birth** — will this be you, Mia Li (DOB 1990-04-05)?\n2. **Checked bags** — as a gold member flying economy, you get 3 free checked bags. How many will you need? (Extra bags are $50 each.)\n3. **Travel insurance** — would you like to add it? It's $30 per passenger and allows a full refund for cancellation due to health or weather reasons.\n4. **Payment method** — you have the following on file:\n   - Visa credit card ending 7447\n   - Visa credit card ending 1907\n   - Travel certificate: $100\n   - Travel certificate: $250\n\n   Which would you like to use? (You can use one certificate + one credit card + up to three gift cards.)"}, "resultat": "Yes, that's my name. I will have 3 checked bags. I do not want travel insurance. I'd like to use my two certificates to pay.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 13, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:43:32.701382Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "One thing to note: each reservation can use **at most one travel certificate**, so I can't apply both. However, I can combine one certificate with a credit card or gift card.\n\nHere are your options for covering the $255 fare:\n\n- **$250 certificate** + $5 on a credit card → note the unused balance of the certificate is forfeited (the $250 fully applies since the fare exceeds $250)\n- **$100 certificate** + $155 on a credit card\n\nWhich certificate would you like to use, and which card (Visa ending 7447 or 1907) should cover the remainder?"}, "resultat": "I'll use the $250 certificate and pay the remaining $5 with my card ending in 7447.", "erreur": null}
